🐛 Describe the bug
layernorm.cpp line 289 ~ line 300 link
In this C++ code, when the input tensor's dtype is bf16, the dtype of eps also changes to bf16. However, the eps dtype passed by the user from the Python frontend is double, which causes eps' value to change during conversion. Typically, the eps value passed by the user when using layernorm in the Python frontend is 1e-5. However, when adding a cout statement here, the eps_val is observed to be 1.00136e-05.
debug code
// output value is 1.00136e-05
std::cout << "static_cast<double>(eps_val) is " << static_cast<double>(eps_val) << std::endl; 
// output value is 1e-5
std::cout << "eps.value() is " << eps.value() << std::endl;
